   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "To understand the concept of Dynamic Programming.\n",
    "To solve the 0/1 Knapsack Problem using Dynamic Programming.\n",
    "To maximize the total profit while satisfying the weight constraint.\n",
    "To analyze the time and space complexity of the algorithm."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da426a26-c289-4cdf-9d64-03e86934f576",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Introduction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a6a10886-33ae-454c-b027-befdaa164c16",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The 0/1 Knapsack Problem is one of the most popular optimization problems in computer science. Given a set of items, each with a weight and a value, the objective is to determine the maximum total value that can be placed into a knapsack with a limited weight capacity.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the 0/1 Knapsack Problem, each item can either be:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Included exactly once (1)\n",
    "    Not included at all (0)\n",
    "\n",
    "Dynamic Programming solves this problem by storing solutions to smaller subproblems and using them to build the final solution efficiently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "19b908eb-c68e-48f5-bbe6-5a24903956f0",
