   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "0/1 Knapsack Problem using Dynamic Programming"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "26b8fe0a-0ffd-4acb-bc36-660b109a3221",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Algorithm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1c1bc8e0-be93-4642-bdc8-5d719c909c79",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "1. Start.\n",
    "2. Read the number of items.\n",
    "3. Read the value and weight of each item.\n",
    "4. Read the capacity of the knapsack.\n",
    "5. Create a Dynamic Programming (DP) table of size (number of items + 1) × (capacity + 1).\n",
    "6. Initialize the first row and first column with zero.\n",
    "7. For each item:\n",
    "    a.If the item's weight is less than or equal to the current capacity:\n",
    "        b.Choose the maximum of:\n",
    "            c.Including the item.\n",
    "            d.Excluding the item.\n",
    "    e.Otherwise, exclude the item.\n",
    "8. Store the maximum value in the DP table.\n",
    "9. Display the maximum profit.\n",
    "10.Stop."
   ]
  },
